# Build output. Everything here is derived from the sources beside it.
build/

# Bundles produced while testing. `apack` writes a directory per application.
dist/
out/

# Packaged artifacts, wherever they land.
#
# `dist/` and `out/` were the only rules, so they only covered packing into the expected
# place. A test run that wrote to a mangled temporary path put two 2.5 MB copies of the
# runtime into the repository as `Userstb918AppDataLocalTemp/...`, and nothing stopped them:
# the directory was neither `dist` nor `out`, and the file was an `.exe`.
#
# These two extensions are the shape of the output, not the shape of the path, so this
# catches a bundle no matter how its destination got mangled. Neither belongs in a source
# tree: `.acvm` is a compiled payload and `.exe` is a copied runtime.
*.exe
*.acvm

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
